PROJECT NAME:
End-to-end UI automation testing for the Sauce Demo website

TECH STACK:
Java25, Maven (Maven Wrapper), Selenium WebDriver, JUnit(Jupiter), AssertJ, Page Object Model

TEST COVERAGE:
1. Smoke test
2. Login: valid login + 4 negative cases (parameterized)
3. Product sorting: name A-Z / Z-A, price low-high/high-low
4. Cart: badge count, remove from cart parge, remove from inventory page
5. End-to-end purchase flow

PROJECT STRUCTURE:
All Page Objects are in pages folder, and each Page is a calss;
BaseTest is for start and close browser;
All tests is classified by functions.

HOW TO RUN:
Prerequisites: JDK 25 and Chrome
Command: ./mvnw test (mvnw.cmd test on Windows)

TEST DESIGN NOTES:
* Using equivalence class partitioning for reverse engineering of login tests

* A–Z sorting tests should first switch to Z–A to avoid
"tests passing even when the functionality is broken"

* Using explicit waits instead of Thread.sleep, and
how to discover and fix unstable tests (such as the Chrome password pop-up issue).

WORK IN PROGRESS:
Checkout tests, screenshots of failures, headless mode, GitHub Actions, and bugs discovered using problem_user.
